sampling handler, creating a new `ChatOpenAI`/`ChatAnthropic` client object on every sampling request. The same pattern appears in `summarizeFileWithFlash` — a new adapter is constructed per file.\n\n```typescript\n// Recreated on every call — allocates new HTTP client, retries config, etc.\nmcp.setSamplingHandler(async (messages, options) => {\n  const { createTierAdapter } = await import(\"../adapters/factory.js\");\n  const adapter = createTierAdapter(\"flash\", container.config); // new client each time\n  ...\n});\n```\n\n**Fix — hoist the adapter outside the handler:**\n\n```typescript\n// In createEngine(), after container is ready:\nconst { createTierAdapter } = await import(\"../adapters/factory.js\");\nconst flashAdapter = createTierAdapter(\"flash\", container.config);\n\nmcp.setSamplingHandler(async (messages, options) => {\n  const { HumanMessage: HM, SystemMessage: SM, AIMessage: AM } = await import(\"@langchain/core/messages\");\n  const lcMessages = messages.map((m) => {\n    if (m.role === \"system\") return new SM(m.content);\n    if (m.role === \"assistant\") return new AM(m.content);\n    return new HM(m.content);\n  });\n  const response = await flashAdapter.client.invoke(lcMessages);\n  return { role: \"assistant\", content: typeof response.content === \"string\" ? response.content : \"\" };\n});\n```\n\nSame fix applies to `summarizeFileWithFlash` — accept a pre-resolved `ResolvedModel` as a parameter instead of creating one per call.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Cache Write on Every Entry — `IndexCache`\n\n**File:** `src/codemap/cache.ts`\n\n`save()` calls `writeFileSync` (a full JSON serialization + disk write) on every `set()`. When indexing a large workspace, this fires N times — once per file.\n\n```typescript\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  this.save(); // full disk write on every single file\n}\n```\n\n**Fix — dirty flag with explicit flush:**\n\n```typescript\nexport class IndexCache {\n  private dirty = false;\n\n  public set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n    this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n    this.dirty = true;\n  }\n\n  public flush(): void {\n    if (!this.dirty) return;\n    const dir = join(this.cachePath, \"..\");\n    if (!existsSync(dir)) mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    writeFileSync(this.cachePath, JSON.stringify(this.data, null, 2));\n    this.dirty = false;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCall `cache.flush()` once after the indexing loop completes rather than inside `set()`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. O(n²) Agent ID Lookup in Startup Validation\n\n**File:** `src/bootstrap/validate.ts`\n\n`allAgentIds` is a plain array, so `allAgentIds.includes(id)` is O(n) per check. Inside `skill.agents.filter(...)`, this becomes O(skills × agents × agentsPerSkill).\n\n```typescript\nconst allAgentIds = [\n  ...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id),\n  ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id),\n];\n// O(n) per lookup\nconst invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !allAgentIds.includes(id));\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```typescript\nconst allAgentIds = new Set([\n  ...agents.listInteractive().map(a => a.id),\n  ...agents.listTask().map(a => a.id),\n]);\n// O(1) per lookup\nconst invalidAgents = skill.agents.filter(id => !allAgentIds.has(id));\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. N+1 File Reads in `validateAssets` + Dynamic `require`\n\n**File:** `src/bootstrap/validate.ts`\n\nEach skill triggers a `require(\"fs\").readFileSync(...)` inside the loop body. The dynamic `require` bypasses the module import at the top of the file and re-resolves the module on every iteration (minor cost, but signals a deeper issue).\n\n```typescript\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  try {\n    // Dynamic require inside hot loop — skill.filePath already read during indexing\n    const raw = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n    ...\n  } catch {}\n}\n```\n\n**Fix** — `skills.indexed` entries were already read from disk during `SkillManager` indexing. The frontmatter keys should be available on the `SkillEntry` object rather than re-reading the file. If `SkillEntry` doesn't expose them yet, add a `rawContent` or `hasTriggers`/`hasAgents`/`hasActive` property during initial indexing, eliminating the re-read entirely. At minimum, replace `require(\"fs\")` with the top-level import.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Unbounded In-Memory Cache Growth\n\n**File:** `src/codemap/cache.ts`\n\n`IndexCache.data` accumulates entries for every indexed file with no eviction. In a large monorepo, this can consume significant memory and the serialized JSON file grows indefinitely.\n\n**Fix — add a max-entries cap with LRU eviction on `set()`:**\n\n```typescript\nprivate readonly MAX_ENTRIES = 5_000;\n\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  if (Object.keys(this.data).length >= this.MAX_ENTRIES) {\n    // evict oldest entry\n    const oldest = Object.entries(this.data)\n      .sort(([, a], [, b]) => a.lastIndexed - b.lastIndexed)[0][0];\n    delete this.data[oldest];\n  }\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  this.dirty = true;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Audit Logger — Synchronous Append Per Event\n\n**File:** `src/logging/audit.ts`\n\n`appendFileSync` opens, writes, and closes the log file on every event. Under high event load (token streaming fires `STREAM_CHUNK_RECEIVED` on every chunk), this is a blocking I/O call per chunk.\n\n```typescript\nprivate write(file: string, entry: LogEntry): void {\n  appendFileSync(file, JSON.stringify(entry) + \"\\n\"); // sync on every chunk\n}\n```\n\n**Fix — buffer with async drain:**\n\n```typescript\nexport class AuditLogger {\n  private localBuffer: string[] = [];\n  private globalBuffer: string[] = [];\n  private flushTimer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | null = null;\n\n  constructor(private opts: AuditLoggerOptions) {\n    ...\n    this.flushTimer = setInterval(() => this.drainBuffers(), 500);\n  }\n\n  private drainBuffers(): void {\n    if (this.localBuffer.length) {\n      appendFileSync(this.localFile, this.localBuffer.join(\"\"));\n      this.localBuffer = [];\n    }\n    if (this.globalBuffer.length) {\n      appendFileSync(this.globalFile, this.globalBuffer.join(\"\"));\n      this.globalBuffer = [];\n    }\n  }\n\n  private writeLocal(entry: LogEntry): void {\n    this.localBuffer.push(JSON.stringify(entry) + \"\\n\");\n  }\n\n  dispose(): void {\n    if (this.flushTimer) clearInterval(this.flushTimer);\n    this.drainBuffers(); // final flush on shutdown\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### No React — Skipping Re-render Analysis\n\nThere is no React code in the provided files. This is a Node.js/TypeScript CLI. The UI layer (if Ink/React-based) wasn't included, so that category doesn't apply to what's shown.\n\n---\n\n## Priority Summary\n\n| Priority | Issue | File | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| High | Timer not cleared in elicitation handler | `bootstrap/cli.ts` | Memory + correctness |\n| High | `IndexCache.save()` on every write | `codemap/cache.ts` | Disk I/O × N files |\n| High | New model adapter per MCP sample | `bootstrap/cli.ts` | Object churn per request |\n| Medium | O(n²) agent ID lookup | `bootstrap/validate.ts` | Startup time |\n| Medium | N+1 file re-reads in validation | `bootstrap/validate.ts` | Startup I/O |\n| Medium | Unbounded cache growth | `codemap/cache.ts` | Memory |\n| Low | `appendFileSync` per log event | `logging/audit.ts` | I/O under load |\n",
